// expect-ok
// Z3 corpus #12: axis-1 expressiveness — non-primitive reassignment.
//
// HISTORY
//
// Through Step 39 of the post-Phase-3 hardening loop, this fixture was
// `expect-error`: the Phase-1 type-checker blanket-rejected reassignment
// of any non-primitive variable with diagnostic T043 ("only primitive
// types support reassignment in Phase 1"). The rejection was strictly
// conservative — non-cap aggregates have no soundness concern — but the
// language couldn't express the M-of-N coordinator pattern, the
// inter-actor 3-of-3 quorum, or any other shape that wanted to swap a
// record / enum value over time.
//
// Wall 1 Step 1 closed the **narrow** case: a new predicate
// `type_is_reassignable` permits reassignment for any type that does
// not transitively own a capability or a borrow. This fixture now
// compiles cleanly. The MUTATION_SITE has moved (see below).
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE STILL DOES NOT EXERCISE
//
// The original M-of-N quorum pattern uses `Option<Cap>` state fields,
// which Step 1 still rejects (cap-containing types remain non-
// reassignable to preserve T183/T184/T186 invariants). Steps 2 and 3
// of the Wall 1 program add a built-in `Slot<Cap>` linear container
// and the corresponding fixtures (`17_m_of_n_quorum.sigil`,
// `18_inter_actor_3_of_3.sigil`).
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// The previous MUTATION_SITE (the reassignment line itself) is no
// longer load-bearing — the fixture compiles whether the reassignment
// is present or absent. The new MUTATION_SITE is the `mut` keyword
// on the `let` binding. Deleting it (turning `let mut h` into `let h`)
// triggers T042 ("cannot assign to immutable variable") rather than
// T043, so the mutation harness has a meaningful inverse: with `mut`,
// fixture compiles; without `mut`, it doesn't. This proves the test
// pins the reassignment code path and not some incidental property
// of the surrounding match / actor / cap declarations.
module sigil;
cap type Fuel {}

enum Holder { Empty, Have(i64) }

fn try_reassign(seed: i64) -> i64 {
    // MUTATION_SITE — `mut` is load-bearing for this fixture's verdict.
    let mut h: Holder = Empty;
    h = Have(seed);
    return seed;
}

entry actor Main {
    state { fuel: Fuel }

    on Start() -> i64 {
        return try_reassign(1);
    }
}
